---Generate a webhook signing secret
---
---Generate a new signing secret for the endpoint, store it, and return it once. Use this for providers where you choose the secret, such as GitHub. It replaces the existing secret. Pass `previousSecretTtlSeconds` to keep accepting the old secret while you update the provider; without it, deliveries signed with the old secret fail verification straight away. Endpoints whose source verifies with a public key refuse this; set the provider's key with the set secret endpoint instead.
---
---`POST /api/v1/webhooks/endpoints/{endpointId}/rotate-secret`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input trigger_dev.RotateWebhookEndpointSecretV1Request
---@return trigger_dev.RotateWebhookEndpointSecretResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:rotate_webhook_endpoint_secret_v1(input) end

---Replay a run
---
---Creates a new run with the same payload and options as the original run, in the same environment. Send a body to override the payload, metadata, or trigger options for the new run. The body is optional; an empty body replays the run unchanged.
---
---`POST /api/v1/runs/{runId}/replay`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input trigger_dev.RunReplayV1Request
---@return trigger_dev.RunReplayV1Response? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:run_replay_v1(input) end

